{"name":"Dream Seascape","hex":"#d5dec3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dream","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Imaginary events seen in the mind while sleeping.","A hope or wish."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To see imaginary events in one's mind while sleeping.","To hope, to wish."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dream"},{"term":"seascape","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A view of the sea.","A piece of art that depicts the sea or shoreline."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seascape"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dream","blocks":[{"text":"A dream is a succession of images, dynamic scenes and situations, ideas, emotions, and sensations that usually occur involuntarily in the mind during certain stages of sleep. Humans generally spend more than two hours dreaming per night, and each dream lasts around 5–20 minutes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/A_dream_%28BM_1868%2C0808.9057%29.jpg/330px-A_dream_%28BM_1868%2C0808.9057%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dream","wikidata":"Q36348"},{"title":"Seascape","blocks":[{"text":"A seascape is a photograph, painting, or other work of art which depicts the sea, in other words an example of marine art. The word originated as a formation from landscape, which was first used for images of land in art. By a similar development, \"seascape\" has also come to mean actual perceptions of the sea itself. It is applied in planning contexts to geographical locations possessing a good view of the sea. Seascape aesthetics receive legal protection in terms of biodiversity/ health of the seas (the OSPAR Convention, and in terms of the visual bio-cultural seascape."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/The_Wave_-_Pierre-Auguste_Renoir_-_Google_Cultural_Institute.jpg/330px-The_Wave_-_Pierre-Auguste_Renoir_-_Google_Cu